{
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "is_hardware_incident",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly identifies the hardware subset the query centers on, enabling incident-rate computation. Values track short_description soundly (software install -> False)."
    },
    {
      "name": "incident_category_group",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Categorization gives a genuine grouping axis and largely overlaps with is_hardware_incident but adds finer granularity (software/database/network). Categories are reasonable readings of the descriptions; note slight redundancy with the boolean but still useful."
    },
    {
      "name": "root_cause_hint",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.95,
      "source_groundedness": 0.65,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "This is the single most query-relevant column: identifying common failure causes is exactly what the analysis needs. However some specific causes (fan_failure, gpu_overload, driver_outdated, overheating) are highly specific inferences that terse short_descriptions likely do not warrant; NULL for silent rows is fine, but the confident specifics risk over-reading."
    },
    {
      "name": "recurrence_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.5,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Recurrence could inform which causes recur, offering some leverage. But groundedness is questionable: the sampled rows expose only short_description and timestamps, and a true/false recurrence flag needs cross-row or caller/config linkage not clearly derivable from a single row's text."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.82,
  "source_groundedness": 0.75,
  "rationale": "The columns collectively map well onto the query: hardware identification (is_hardware_incident/incident_category_group) plus root_cause_hint enable estimating how addressing top causes lowers the hardware incident rate. Groundedness is generally sound for categorization from short_description, but root_cause_hint's specific mechanical causes and the recurrence_signal flag exceed what terse single-row text reliably supports, indicating some over-confident inference."
}

